[[File:Azealia Banks 2012 NME Awards cropped.jpg|left|upright|thumb|[[Azealia Banks]] (2012), one of several rappers who remixed the song]]

On February 14, 2013, American rapper [[Azealia Banks]] released a [[remix]] to "Harlem Shake" on [[SoundCloud]],<ref name="Zoladz">{{cite web|last=Zoladz|first=Lindsay|date=February 15, 2013|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/49582-baauer-gets-azealia-banks-harlem-shake-taken-down-feels-her-twitter-wrath/|title=Baauer Gets Azealia Banks' "Harlem Shake" Taken Down, Feels Her Twitter Wrath|work=Pitchfork|access-date=February 18, 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130218001337/http://pitchfork.com/news/49582-baauer-gets-azealia-banks-harlem-shake-taken-down-feels-her-twitter-wrath/|archive-date=February 18, 2013|url-status=live}}</ref> which was then removed at Baauer's request. Banks disparaged Baauer on [[Twitter]] in response and claimed to have e-mails sent from him giving her permission to use the song. She then said that Diplo had sent her an e-mail telling her that the remix was removed because they would rather have rapper [[Juicy J]] on it.<ref name="Battan">{{cite web|last=Battan|first=Carrie|date=February 18, 2013|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/49604-baauer-explains-azealia-banks-harlem-shake-squabble-working-with-alunageorge-on-new-ep/|title=Baauer Explains Azealia Banks "Harlem Shake" Squabble, Working With AlunaGeorge on New EP|work=Pitchfork|access-date=February 18, 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130220184153/http://pitchfork.com/news/49604-baauer-explains-azealia-banks-harlem-shake-squabble-working-with-alunageorge-on-new-ep/|archive-date=February 20, 2013|url-status=live}}</ref> On February 16, Banks shared a [[music video]] for her remix on [[Vimeo]],<ref>{{cite web|last=Minsker|first=Evan|date=February 16, 2013|url=https://pitchfork.com/news/49587-azealia-banks-shares-her-harlem-shake-video/|title=Azealia Banks Shares Her "Harlem Shake" Video, Claims She Got Baauer's Permission to Use Track|work=Pitchfork|access-date=February 18, 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130220184128/http://pitchfork.com/news/49587-azealia-banks-shares-her-harlem-shake-video/|archive-date=February 20, 2013|url-status=live}}</ref> and revealed a purported e-mail from Baauer saying he liked the remix.<ref name="Caramanica"/> Baauer responded in an interview for ''[[The Daily Beast]]'', saying that they had planned to release a version of the song with Banks, but felt that her verse did not meet their expectations:

{{Centered pull quote|She laid something on 'Harlem Shake' and it was so/so. Didn't love it. And that was a little while ago, and since all this video stuff happened, our plans all changed. Because of that, we decided to just release the song on its own with no vocal version. So we told her, 'Please don't release your version.' And she said, 'Well, I'm going to put it online anyway.' And we said, 'Please don't. We'd really like it if you didn't.' And she did.<ref name="Battan"/>}}

Jon Caramanica of ''The New York Times'' cited Banks' remix as one of her best songs,<ref name="Caramanica"/> while Chris Martins of ''[[Spin (magazine)|Spin]]'' wrote that she delivers "fire-hot verse after fire-hot verse" and facetiously remarked that "Banks raps all over your dumb 'Harlem Shake' meme".<ref>{{cite journal|last=Martins|first=Chris|date=February 14, 2013|url=https://www.spin.com/2013/02/azealia-banks-harlem-shake-baauer-remix-rap/|title=Azealia Banks Raps All Over Your Dumb 'Harlem Shake' Meme|journal=[[Spin (magazine)|Spin]]|location=New York|access-date=February 20, 2013|archive-url=https://archive.today/20240526130914/https://www.webcitation.org/6EaS56Vod?url=http://m.spin.com/entry/view/id/26882%3FKSID=b7675e7990a78cb781f09ba4e13abf52|archive-date=May 26, 2024|url-status=live}}</ref>

[[Pitbull (entertainer)|Pitbull]] and [[Jim Jones (rapper)|Jim Jones]] also recorded [[freestyle rap]]s over the song.<ref>{{cite web|date=February 27, 2013|url=http://www.hiphopdx.com/index/singles/id.23740/title.jim-jones-harlem-shake-freestyle-|title=Jim Jones – Harlem Shake Freestyle|publisher=HipHop DX|access-date=March 7, 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130303014138/http://www.hiphopdx.com/index/singles/id.23740/title.Jim+Jones-Harlem+Shake+Freestyle|archive-date=March 3, 2013|url-status=dead}}</ref> After releasing his version, Jones claimed in an interview that "Harlem Shake" was a song he originally recorded one year ago for an album by [[Pauly D]], but that they ultimately scrapped it: "When I started to hear the 'Harlem Shake' and heard the beat, I was like damn, I had the record for a year. So I just put the record out."<ref>{{cite web|last=Horowitz|first=Steven J.|date=March 7, 2013|url=http://www.hiphopdx.com/index/news/id.23122/title.jim-jones-says-baauer-s-harlem-shake-was-originally-his-record/|title=Jim Jones Says Baauer's "Harlem Shake" Was Originally His Record|publisher=HipHopDX|access-date=March 7, 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130310042510/http://www.hiphopdx.com/index/news/id.23122/title.jim-jones-says-baauer-s-harlem-shake-was-originally-his-record|archive-date=March 10, 2013|url-status=dead}}</ref>
